'' TB-001, RUN: a type in a module's interface is the module's own wherever it sits there.
'' std/tasks declares 'InterruptContext( ) as Context' (interrupt.tiko) above 'type Context'
'' (sync.tiko), and the declared-below walk bound Win32's CONTEXT instead: TKO0811 with
'' windows.bi or sys/win after the import, the wrong result type silently with sys/win first.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -mt -i toolchains/tiko-windows/inc tests/modules/src/taskswin/syswin-after.tiko -o tests/modules/taskswinsyswinafter.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0811
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/modules/taskswinsyswinafter.exe
'' RUN: tests/modules/taskswinsyswinafter.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: -1
